---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How MyRideSG collects, uses and protects your data — what the app records about you and your motorcycle, who it is shared with, and your choices over it."
  meta="Last updated: 6 August 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    MyRide SG ("we", "us", or "our") operates the MyRide SG web application (the
    "Service"), accessible at <strong>myridesg.com</strong>. This Privacy Policy
    explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you
    use our Service. By using the Service, you agree to the collection and use of
    information in accordance with this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Account Information:</strong> When you sign in with Google, we receive your
    name, email address, and profile picture from Google. We do not receive your Google
    password.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>User-Generated Data:</strong> Information you voluntarily enter into the
    Service, including motorcycle details (make, model, plate number), maintenance logs,
    fuel fill-up records, mileage readings, expense records, and document expiry dates
    (COE, insurance, road tax).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Usage Data:</strong> We may collect information about how the Service is
    accessed and used, including your device type, browser type, pages viewed, and time
    spent on pages.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide, operate, and maintain the Service</li>
    <li>To authenticate your identity and manage your account</li>
    <li>To store and display your motorcycle and maintenance data</li>
    <li>To send service reminders and expiry alerts you have opted into</li>
    <li>To calculate and display fuel efficiency, cost per km, and spending analytics</li>
    <li>To operate the XP rewards and gamification system</li>
    <li>To improve and personalise the Service</li>
    <li>To communicate important updates about the Service</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Usage Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We record how riders move through the app — which screens are opened, which features
    are used, and where a form is abandoned — so we can find what is confusing or broken
    and fix it. We rely on the Business Improvement exception under Singapore's Personal
    Data Protection Act for this.
  </p>
  <p>
    These records never contain your name, email address, phone number, vehicle plate
    number, NRIC, location, or anything you typed into the app. They are stored in our
    own database and are never sold or shared with advertisers or other companies.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep this data for 180 days, after which it is deleted automatically. You can turn
    it off at any time under Account → Share usage data, and deleting your account
    removes the link between these records and you.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Google Sign-In</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google OAuth 2.0 to authenticate users. When you sign in with Google, we
    access only your basic profile information (name and email address) as permitted by
    the scopes you authorise. We do not access your Gmail, Google Drive, Google Contacts,
    or any other Google service data. Your use of Google Sign-In is also governed by <a
      href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information to third parties. We may
    share data in the following limited circumstances:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service Providers:</strong> Third-party vendors who assist us in operating
      the Service (e.g., cloud hosting, analytics) under confidentiality agreements.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> If required by law, regulation, or valid legal
      process.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business Transfer:</strong> In the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale
      of assets, user data may be transferred with appropriate notice.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain your personal data for as long as your account is active. You can delete
    your account and associated data at any time, in-app, at <strong
      >Account → Delete account</strong
    > — no need to contact support. Deletion is immediate and cannot be undone; some records
    may be retained where required by Singapore law. You may also request deletion by contacting
    us at <strong>hello@myridesg.com</strong> if you prefer.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We implement industry-standard security measures to protect your data, including
    encrypted connections (HTTPS/TLS), access controls, and secure cloud infrastructure.
    However, no method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure, and we cannot
    guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your data</li>
    <li>
      Withdraw consent at any time by disconnecting Google Sign-In and deleting your
      account
    </li>
    <li>
      Lodge a complaint with the Personal Data Protection Commission (PDPC) of Singapore
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <strong>hello@myridesg.com</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
  <p>
    We use browser local storage and session cookies to maintain your login session and
    application preferences (e.g., theme, settings). We do not use third-party
    advertising cookies. You may clear cookies and local storage through your browser
    settings, which will log you out of the Service.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is not directed to individuals under the age of 16. We do not knowingly
    collect personal data from children under 16. If you believe we have inadvertently
    collected such data, please contact us immediately and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of
    significant changes by updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.
    Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing Law</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy is governed by the laws of Singapore, including the Personal Data
    Protection Act 2012 (PDPA). Any disputes shall be subject to the exclusive
    jurisdiction of the courts of Singapore.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:</p>
  <p>
    <strong>MyRide SG</strong><br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:hello@myridesg.com">hello@myridesg.com</a><br />
    Website: <a href="https://myridesg.com">https://myridesg.com</a><br />
    Singapore
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
